          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Career and Teaching</strong><br>\nAfter winning the Nobel Prize, Brattain remained active in research and also became a respected teacher. He was known for encouraging young scientists and made a significant contribution to the training of the next generation of physicists.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Interests</strong><br>\nIn addition to his scientific career, Brattain had a fulfilling personal life. He was a passionate hiker and nature lover, often venturing into the mountains. He combined his love for nature with a deep understanding of physics, which he enjoyed sharing with young people in his free time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nWalter Brattain's legacy lives on in the incredible variety of electronic devices that are now part of our daily lives. His work laid the foundations for the information society and the development of modern technologies. Brattain left behind a world that was significantly changed by his inventions.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
